WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.748
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:02.881 --> 00:06.802
Let's curate a new gene, step by step.

00:07.300 --> 00:12.800
<i>MAU2</i> had no SysNDD entity when we recorded this.

00:12.934 --> 00:16.741
How do you create one, and which category does it earn?

00:17.233 --> 00:20.484
In the Curation menu, select Create entity.

00:20.617 --> 00:24.219
In Gene, type <i>MAU2</i> and select it.

00:24.352 --> 00:31.352
In Disease, type Cornelia de Lange,
and select syndrome 7, the <i>MAU2</i> subtype.

00:31.967 --> 00:36.517
In Inheritance, select Autosomal dominant inheritance.

00:36.650 --> 00:41.371
Cognitive impairment is common,
so this is a neurodevelopmental disorder,

00:41.505 --> 00:45.486
or NDD: set NDD Phenotype to Yes.

00:45.619 --> 00:51.487
Gene, mode of inheritance and
disease define the entity: check them now.

00:52.000 --> 00:57.207
Under Publications, add the cohort study,
an independent case report

00:57.341 --> 00:59.158
and the first report.

00:59.291 --> 01:03.812
Leave out the preprint; its journal version replaces it.

01:03.946 --> 01:08.559
In GeneReviews, add the Cornelia de Lange chapter.

01:09.067 --> 01:15.655
In Synopsis, give counts:
about 19 individuals from 16 families,

01:15.788 --> 01:18.480
9 with <i>de novo</i> variants.

01:18.614 --> 01:22.943
Add variant types, the range of intellectual disability,

01:23.076 --> 01:26.345
and main features with frequencies.

01:26.833 --> 01:31.389
In Phenotypes, search for a term, such as Short stature.

01:31.523 --> 01:34.594
Then tick the modifier present.

01:35.100 --> 01:41.197
Record the features seen
in 20 percent or more of affected individuals.

01:41.330 --> 01:46.512
Intellectual disability varies widely,
from borderline to severe,

01:46.645 --> 01:50.379
so select all four severity terms.

01:50.867 --> 01:56.079
Under Variation Ontology,
select the reported variant types.

01:56.212 --> 02:01.011
Add an effect only where it was shown,
such as protein loss of function

02:01.144 --> 02:04.866
or effect on protein interaction.

02:05.367 --> 02:07.534
Definitive needs a publication,

02:07.667 --> 02:11.975
plus either a clear-cut
frequency or cumulative evidence.

02:12.109 --> 02:16.875
For <i>de novo</i> variants,
clear-cut means 10 or more cases.

02:17.008 --> 02:21.687
<i>MAU2</i> has 9, so it is not met.

02:22.200 --> 02:24.467
Cumulative evidence is met.

02:24.601 --> 02:28.939
9 <i>de novo</i> cases meet a strong frequency criterion.

02:29.072 --> 02:31.448
A <i>de novo</i> truncating variant in a gene

02:31.581 --> 02:36.000
intolerant to loss of function
meets a strong genetic one.

02:36.134 --> 02:38.926
So the entity is Definitive.

02:39.433 --> 02:42.687
In Status, select Definitive.

02:42.820 --> 02:48.355
In Comment, give your reasons and your doubts:
most cases come from one cohort,

02:48.488 --> 02:52.184
and two variants had no effect in any assay.

02:52.317 --> 02:55.433
These doubts could justify Moderate.

02:55.933 --> 02:59.692
In Review & Submit, check the summary.

03:00.200 --> 03:04.568
Leave Direct approval off, and select Submit Entity.

03:04.702 --> 03:09.080
A second Curator approves it before it is public.

03:09.567 --> 03:14.925
Remember:
gene, mode of inheritance and disease define the entity.

03:15.059 --> 03:17.576
The criteria decide the category.

03:17.710 --> 03:21.568
And record only what the papers support.

03:22.067 --> 03:27.826
Read more in the documentation
chapter called Create an entity.
